      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massillon%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named after French bishop Jean‑Baptiste Massillon at his wife's request.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massillon%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Rotch and his wife used their farmhouse as a stop on the Underground Railroad.",
